= Labour and Socialist International

We are an important part of the current Socialist International. We can try out a few things. 

(Note: This doesn't do anything yet)

- @increase_founding: Put party resources into the International
- @colonial_stance: Work towards a clear position on Colonialism
- @comintern_relation: Improve relations with the Comintern
- @fourth_relation: Improve relation with the Trotskyist Fourth International



@increase_founding
subtitle: This organ is severly underfounded compared to the ammount of it's membership.


We are still laking behind the Comintern's resources founded by the Soviet Union.


@colonial_stance
subtitle: Our organisation can't agitate coherently on the colonial question.

- @british: Support the British position
- @austrian: Support the Austrian position
- @french: Support the French position


@british
subtitle: The colonial administration should be reformed but it is not sensible to give them independence (in the near future).

@french
subtitle: What position?

@austrian
subtitle: Colonies should be abolished, self-determination for all.


@comintern_relation
subtitle: We should not be rivals, we have more in common than we want to admit.


@fourth_relation
subtitle: They aren't that influential.










 


  
